WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:04.565
Start with the approved ZTF Orchestrator appliance image and its checksum.

00:00:04.907 --> 00:00:08.597
Verify the download, then import the image as a disk in Prism.

00:00:08.745 --> 00:00:13.140
Create the virtual machine, put the imported disk first in the boot order, and

00:00:13.183 --> 00:00:16.660
connect its network adapter to the approved management subnet.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.434
Leave the machine powered off while you set up access.

00:00:19.989 --> 00:00:24.362
On your Windows workstation, open Command Prompt and run the commands shown.

00:00:24.682 --> 00:00:28.394
Choose a filename you have never used before and protect the private key with a

00:00:28.437 --> 00:00:29.205
passphrase.

00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:32.308
The file ending in dot pub is your public key.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.920
Copy its entire line for the appliance.

00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:37.438
Keep the private key on your workstation.

00:00:37.758 --> 00:00:41.023
If your team issued a key, use the approved key instead.

00:00:41.582 --> 00:00:46.702
In your approved AHV guest customization or cloud-init user data field, enter

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.153
the example from the guide.

00:00:48.451 --> 00:00:53.113
It creates the Linux account named Z T F admin and adds your public key.

00:00:53.422 --> 00:00:56.920
Replace the entire example key line and keep the indentation.

00:00:57.219 --> 00:01:01.016
If your site uses its own access profile, have the provisioning administrator

00:01:01.187 --> 00:01:01.848
apply it.

00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:04.580
Save the customization before powering on the machine.

00:01:05.137 --> 00:01:08.743
Find the appliance address in Prism or your DHCP records.

00:01:08.977 --> 00:01:12.647
Replace the example address in the SSH command with that address.

00:01:12.988 --> 00:01:16.542
Verify the server fingerprint with your administrator before accepting it.

00:01:16.853 --> 00:01:20.778
When you get a Linux prompt, run who am I and sudo dash V.

00:01:21.077 --> 00:01:24.995
You should see the Z T F admin username and a successful sudo check.

00:01:25.287 --> 00:01:29.724
If SSH says permission denied, check the username and matching key before

00:01:29.895 --> 00:01:33.209
asking the provisioning administrator to review guest customization.

00:01:33.778 --> 00:01:36.475
Keep DHCP if your site uses a reservation.

00:01:36.825 --> 00:01:41.475
For a static address, use a working Prism console login or ask the provisioning

00:01:41.561 --> 00:01:43.481
administrator to set it at the source.

00:01:43.907 --> 00:01:47.833
Follow the Quick Guide to identify the adapter, back up the Netplan file, and

00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:48.698
try the change.

00:01:49.051 --> 00:01:52.763
Reconnect over SSH at the intended address before keeping it.

00:01:53.019 --> 00:01:57.414
If access fails, let the trial expire and restore the saved configuration from

00:01:57.457 --> 00:01:58.148
the console.

00:01:58.507 --> 00:02:02.816
In your verified Linux session, check that the Orchestrator and PostgreSQL

00:02:02.902 --> 00:02:06.656
containers are running and that the local health endpoint reports healthy.

00:02:06.998 --> 00:02:09.524
Search the service journal for the first-run banner.

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:13.416
If there is no match, check the container log with the second command on

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:14.034
screen.

00:02:14.312 --> 00:02:17.682
Look for username admin and the generated password underneath.

00:02:17.981 --> 00:02:20.977
That password is for the Z T F web console.

00:02:21.242 --> 00:02:25.423
If both logs are empty and the app is healthy, ask the appliance owner to

00:02:25.466 --> 00:02:26.618
recover the web account.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:31.396
Open the approved appliance address in your browser, sign in as admin, and

00:02:31.439 --> 00:02:35.161
change the generated password under Administration, Users.

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:38.605
Confirm the installed build in Settings, About.

00:02:38.882 --> 00:02:42.722
Record the management address and health result, and keep credentials in the

00:02:42.765 --> 00:02:43.697
approved store.
